ng when passing  urine  contact your surgeon if you have any  questions about your foley catheter your  temperature is 101 degrees fahrenheit or  higher  your bladder feels full but you see no  urine draining into the foley bag  you cannot remove your catheter with  gentle pulling  your urine is cloudy has a foul odor or  you see a lot of blood in your urine  it is normal to see a small amount of  blood in your urine after removing a  foley catheter  also contact your surgeon if you cannot  urinate within eight hours after  removing the foley catheter  you feel burning or pain when urinating  that lasts longer than 24 hours your  stomach feels bloated or painful  you feel the need to urinate more often  than normal  or your bladder doesn't feel empty after  urinating
 

